            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.cpp",
                    "line": 600,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "If I'm understanding this correctly, this callback will be called for every systemd job that gets started. It seems (?) like that might be frequent?\n\nIf so, maybe poweroffTarget should be a data member so it doesn't have to be constantly rebuilt?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.cpp",
                    "line": 600,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, an earlier comment in these reviews was to just hard code the target file as a const since SMP will only ever be dealing with intance 0, so I'll just use that const value."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.cpp",
                    "line": 611,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Just curious. I thought this target might have some sort of systemd dependency that would have caused the chassis-specific power off targets to be called automatically, avoiding the need to do it in C++? I'm probably just not understanding how this all works."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.cpp",
                    "line": 611,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, I responded to a similar question in an earlier review but basically I did not add those dependencies in the systemd targets and chose to coordinate it via this new SMP application. If I did it via systemd then this app would be getting notifications for each of the chassis and it would introduce a lot of complexity in the code. Basically I had 2 choices, do it all via systemd, or do it via this app. Mixing the 2 would be dangerous."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.hpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Nit: Missing blank line as separator?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.hpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.hpp",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Unless you intend to inspect matches later, you could probably use a single vector of match objects named matches. I'm not sure they need to be separated by purpose."
                },
                {
                    "file": "chassis_state_manager_smp.hpp",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Personal preference is to just keep them separate but if you feel strongly feel free to reopen this comment."
                }
            ],
